== The CUDA-13 (1.32.0) provider-only bundle in Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5, 2026-11-27 ==
# Why this file exists: packaging-and-install.md claimed this run and cited the
# import table (onnx-provider-cuda13-deps.log) instead of a transcript, so the
# claim had no artifact. Re-run to give it one.
#
# Build: ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=.validation/ort-gpu-1.32.0,
# OFXPLUGIN_BUNDLE_CUDA_PROVIDER=ON, OFXPLUGIN_CUDA_FROM_HOST=ON,
# OFXPLUGIN_HOST_CUDA_MAJOR=13 -> four files, provider imports cuBLAS 13,
# gate "--require-cuda-major 13": verdict: every gate asked for passed.
#
# The machine has the CUDA 13.0 toolkit on PATH
# (C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v13.0\bin\x64), so
# cublas64_13.dll resolves from there and NOT from Resolve. This is a
# contaminated environment, not Resolve accepting CUDA 13: on a host that
# offers only the CUDA 12 it ships, the same provider fails at load (1114).

